* ============================================================
* Self-test: verify LogNormal(stream,0,1.109400,1.085659)
* gives mean ~= 2.0 and CV ~= 1.5 (std.dev ~= 3.0) in THIS GPSS World.
*
* Run this FIRST, before the main cross-validation model.
* If MEAN and STD.DEV don't come out close to 2.0 / 3.0, the
* Scale/Shape arguments need adjusting for your version.
* ============================================================
           SIMULATE

SVC        TABLE   P1,0.25,0.25,80

* Deterministic arrival spacing (1 time unit) - only used to draw
* 100,000 independent LogNormal samples; timing is irrelevant here.
* CORRECTED: this GPSS World's LogNormal(stream,Locate,Scale,Shape)
* = Locate + exp(Scale + Shape*Z), i.e. Scale is used ADDITIVELY as
* mu (not as exp(mu)). mu = ln(2) - sigma^2/2 = 0.103820.
           GENERATE 1,,,100000
           ASSIGN   1,(LogNormal(1,0,0.103820,1.085659))
           TABULATE SVC
           TERMINATE 1

           START    100000
